  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Ghana: Cold Chain Facilities Network, through Global Cold Chain Alliance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant to FreezeLink 3PL, Limited funds a feasibility study (FS) to assess the deployment of a temperature-controlled logistics network consisting of multiple storage facilities and services within Ghana. The network would likely consist of facilities at the major port of Tema and the largest Ghanaian cities, as well as mid and smaller sized cities. The envisioned cold chain network will facilitate the storage of imported and locally-produced refrigerated and frozen agricultural commodities, including meats, fruits, and vegetables, with a significant focus on poultry broiler meat. The U.S. company World Food Logistics Organization has been selected to carry out the Study on a sole-source basis.</narrative>
  </description>
